## Example configurations

These starter values mirror the deployment patterns used by `docker-compose.yml`, `docker-compose.prod.yml`, and `docker-compose.noproxy.prod.yml`.

### Node-only development

```yaml
mode: dev
profiles:
  node:
    enabled: true
  portal:
    enabled: false

initData:
  enabled: true
  inputData:
    hostPath:
      enabled: true
      path: /path/to/jsonld
      type: Directory

storage:
  graphdbHome:
    type: hostPath
    hostPath:
      path: /tmp/neurobagel/graphdb-home
      type: DirectoryOrCreate
  neurobagelData:
    type: hostPath
    hostPath:
      path: /tmp/neurobagel/neurobagel-data
      type: DirectoryOrCreate

routing:
  ingress:
    enabled: false
```

### Portal-only development

```yaml
mode: dev
profiles:
  node:
    enabled: false
  portal:
    enabled: true

initData:
  enabled: false

localNodes:
  - NodeName: Local graph 1
    ApiURL: http://host.docker.internal:8000

routing:
  ingress:
    enabled: false
```

### Production ingress with TLS

```yaml
mode: prod
profiles:
  node:
    enabled: true
  portal:
    enabled: true

initData:
  enabled: true
  inputData:
    hostPath:
      enabled: true
      path: /srv/neurobagel/input
      type: Directory

routing:
  hosts:
    napi: napi.example.org
    fapi: fapi.example.org
    query: query.example.org
  basePaths:
    napi: /
    fapi: /
    query: /
  ingress:
    enabled: true
    className: nginx
    tls:
      enabled: true
      secretName: neurobagel-tls
      clusterIssuer: letsencrypt-prod

storage:
  graphdbHome:
    type: pvc
    size: 20Gi
  neurobagelData:
    type: pvc
    size: 5Gi
```

For runnable test overlays, see `charts/neurobagel/tests/values`.

